(def not-page "(not value)\n\nReturns the opposite of a `bool`.\n\nIt emits `!value`.\n\n(not true)\n=> false")
(def cond-page "(cond (test body ...) clause ...)\n\nRuns the first clause whose test is true.\n\nA last clause `(else body ...)` runs when no test is true. Without one,\nevery body must return unit, and so does the call.\n\n(cond ((> 7 9) \"high\") ((> 7 5) \"middle\") (else \"low\"))\n=> \"middle\"")
